      "commit": "5cfc54e9687684cf8eeec53194dfabff9caef58d",
      "source_file": "src/sqllens/tools/query_database.py",
      "claim_text": "The new `await _conversation_baseline(...)` runs inside the per-conversation turn context manager but outside the `try` block that owns the function's error taxonomy, so exceptions from an embedder-supplied user_resolver or conversation_store reach the MCP client as a raw exception string instead of the sanitized _INTERNAL_ERROR_MESSAGE the docstring promises.",
      "evidence": "Confirmed at source: the baseline await sits inside `async with _conversation_turn(...)` but above the `try` that owns the taxonomy, and src/sqllens/server.py:368 wraps the tool call with only `except AgentRunError`. Fixed by wrapping the baseline call in `except Exception` -> logger.exception + raise RuntimeError(_INTERNAL_ERROR_MESSAGE), the same idiom the sibling paths at lines 388 and 442 use. CancelledError is a BaseException and so is unaffected."
    }
  ],
