  "phase3_findings": [
    {
      "finding_id": "F-1",
      "file": "src/sqllens/tools/query_database.py",
      "line_range": [
        400,
        406
      ],
      "kind": "unhandled_exception",
      "severity": "important",
      "agent": "prflow:silent-failure-hunter, prflow:requesting-code-review",
      "description": "The new `await _conversation_baseline(...)` runs inside the per-conversation turn context manager but outside the `try` block at line 408 that owns the function's error taxonomy. Its two awaits, `agent.user_resolver.resolve_user` and `agent.conversation_store.get_conversation`, have no handler, so anything they raise passes `server.py` (which only intercepts `AgentRunError`) and reaches the MCP client as a raw exception string instead of the sanitized `_INTERNAL_ERROR_MESSAGE` the docstring at lines 332-334 promises. Unreachable with the shipped `_StaticUserResolver` and `BoundedConversationStore`, both of which are trivial and cannot raise; an embedder-supplied resolver or store reaches it. The sibling rollback path guards this same seam.",
      "corroboration_count": 2,
      "fix_decision": "applied"
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-2",
      "file": "docs/internal/database-connectors/cleanup-error-handling.md",
      "line_range": [
        41,
        41
      ],
      "kind": "comment_drift",
      "severity": "suggestion",
      "agent": "prflow:comment-analyzer, prflow:requesting-code-review",
      "description": "The sentence \"the cleanup in the `finally:` above still runs on that same thread, before the exception surfaces at the `await`\" holds for an exception raised inside the threaded body but is false for the cancellation case the same paragraph describes. Because `asyncio.to_thread` cannot interrupt a running worker, a `CancelledError` surfaces at the `await` immediately while the thread's `finally` cleanup runs later. Capped behavior-inert by Phase 4.1.5 (first-conjunct held, limb-one held, limb-two held).",
      "corroboration_count": 2
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-3",
      "file": "src/sqllens/agent/integrations/sqlite/sql_runner.py",
      "line_range": [
        143,
        146
      ],
      "kind": "comment_drift",
      "severity": "suggestion",
      "agent": "prflow:comment-analyzer",
      "description": "The inline comment repeats the same imprecision: \"teardown runs on the thread that owns the connection, before any exception surfaces at the await\". The thread-affinity half is correct; the \"before any exception surfaces at the await\" half is false under cancellation. The MySQL and Postgres runners carry no equivalent sentence. Capped behavior-inert by Phase 4.1.5.",
      "corroboration_count": 1
    },
